# ARC-0008 stage 5 (level 9): Succession, Wheel of Ixion, Master of Coin, Master of Ships.
# Spec: 50_ENGINEERING/55_Implementation_Specs/SPEC_ARC-0008.md (stage 5). Applied with
#   perl 80_TOOLS_AND_PIPELINE/82_Automation/stats/stats_add.pl <this> --apply      ([fechado] ARC-0008)
# No `using`: every field is written. Numbers: 25.01/SPL_Kingmaker_WheelOfIxion (level 5, line 18 x 2 m, 5d6 Fire, fire surface
# 2 turns; +1d6 at slot 6 by gen_upcast_variants), 25.02/FEAT_Kingmaker_Succession (9 m), 25.02/FEAT_Kingmaker_Court
# (master_of_ships_radius 9, master_of_coin_uses 1 per Long Rest).

@loca KM_SUCCESSION_NAME Succession
@loca KM_SUCCESSION_DESC When an enemy on the Wheel dies, the nearest enemy within [1] that isn't on the Wheel takes its place, in the same position. The king is dead - long live the king.
@loca KM_IXION_NAME Wheel of Ixion
@loca KM_IXION_DESC Send a burning wheel rolling through your foes and bind them to Fortune's wheel, Falling.
@loca KM_IXION_EXTRA Enemies that succeed the <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throw</LSTag> take half damage but still join the Wheel. The wheel leaves a trail of fire behind it - allies included.
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_COIN_NAME Master of Coin
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_COIN_STATUS Once per <LSTag Tooltip="LongRest">Long Rest</LSTag>, hitting a Fallen enemy returns a spell slot to the Kingmaker.
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_COIN_SPELL Appoint an ally as Master of Coin. Once per <LSTag Tooltip="LongRest">Long Rest</LSTag>, when it hits a Fallen enemy, you regain a spell slot.
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_SHIPS_NAME Master of Ships
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_SHIPS_STATUS Carries the Crossing across the field: an enemy within [1] that becomes Fallen suffers its Crossing as if a Reigning ally stood beside it.
@loca KM_MASTER_OF_SHIPS_SPELL Appoint an ally as Master of Ships. An enemy within [1] of it that becomes Fallen suffers its Crossing as if a Reigning ally stood beside it.
@loca KM_COURT_LEVEL9_NAME The Court: third circle

